  "shortName": null,
  "description": "FurryEST is a furry camping mini-convention in Estonia, organized by Clanga, EndWorld and Renno, with a website by Sanqui. It is held on barge houses near the village of Kabala. It began as an Estonian Summer Furmeet on July 6 to 8, 2018, with 36 people, and the first FurryEST was held in July 2019 with 65. After a two-year pandemic break it returned in 2022, and its 2024 edition filled its cap of 130 attendees within five minutes of registration opening.",
